WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:36.420
<b>Gray Terminal</b>

3
00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:36.920
[NARRATOR]
but the path that led Luffy
to Marineford began long ago.

4
00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.790
Ten years ago, in fact,
in the East Blue.

5
00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:46.060
There lies a small town,
known as Windmill Village,

6
00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:49.200
where people lived
quiet, peaceful lives.

7
00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.000
But it was the nearby Mount Corvo,
where few would dare to set foot.

8
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.710
For only the strong could
survive in its dark woods,

9
00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:01.210
faced with beasts that would
make quick work of trespassers.

10
00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:06.220
[LUFFY]
What's wrong with being
king of the pirates, Grandpa?

11
00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:08.860
Pirates are cool!

12
00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:10.800
And what makes you think I care?

13
00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.010
[LUFFY]
I'm gonna slap you!

14
00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.710
[GARP]
Eating that Devil Fruit
wasn't enough trouble for you?

15
00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.010
Now this nonsense?

16
00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:22.050
<b>Monkey D. Garp








(10 Years Ago)</b>

17
00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.130
You, and your big brother Ace,

18
00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.200
are both going to become fine
Marines, you understand me?

19
00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:26.830
<b>Monkey D. Luffy








(10 Years Ago)</b>

20
00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.900
Ow, ow, ow you suck!

21
00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:26.170
I thought I was supposed to
be made outta rubber now...

22
00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.910
why does this still hurt so much?

23
00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:30.780
[GARP]
I thought leaving you in a nice village

24
00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:33.310
would keep you safe,
but pirates won't be satisfied

25
00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.280
until they get their grubby
hands on everything!

26
00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.540
What's this dump?

27
00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.180
Hey, shut the hell up!

28
00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:46.480
Whatever it is you're sellin',
I don't want none!

29
00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:47.420
[GARP]
Dadan.

30
00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.020
Huh?!

31
00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.520
[shrieks]

32
00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.290
Garp! What are you doin' here?!

33
00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:58.280
<b>Curly Dadan</b>

34
00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:01.720
<b>Dogra, a Mountain Bandit</b>

35
00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.190
<b>Magra, a Mountain Bandit</b>

36
00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:06.600
[GARP]
Charming as ever.

37
00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.070
Sorry for the cold welcome, but I hope

38
00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:11.970
you don't have another
ridiculous favor to ask us!

39
00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:14.440
You realize Ace is already ten, right?

40
00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.510
[GARP]
Oh, is he now?

41
00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.170
And how's the little scamp doing?

42
00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:17.940
Good?

43
00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.940
Well, he's a handful, of course!

44
00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.240
And we've been watching
over the brat for long enough!

45
00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.840
So just take him away!

46
00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:24.740
[GARP]
Never mind.

47
00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.900
Yeah, that's the problem...we do mind!

48
00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:29.200
And speaking of brats,
would you shut that one up?

49
00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.000
He's yours now.

50
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.630
[DADAN]
Huh?

51
00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:34.600
Hey, Luffy, tell 'em hello.

52
00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:35.410
Yo!

53
00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.150
Wait a sec, who is he?

54
00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.980
He's my... grandson.

55
00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:44.000
[DADAN, MAGRA, DOGRA]
Huh?! What?!

56
00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.270
[DOGRA]
I never heard about this!

57
00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:49.640
[DADAN]
And you want us to take care of the little
monster, uh, little darling, I mean.

58
00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.140
Well, no way!

59
00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:51.910
Fine.

60
00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.240
Then I'll give you two choices:

61
00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:57.100
You can either raise my grandson
or spend your life in prison.

62
00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.690
Pretty generous, considering
all the crimes you've committed.

63
00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.230
[laughs]

64
00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.100
No fair!

65
00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.970
The thing is, I'd rather
stay outta the slammer.

66
00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:09.910
Frankly, if you asked me
that on one of Ace's bad days,

67
00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.440
I might have to go for
the prison option after all.

68
00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:13.480
And two brats?

69
00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.100
Yeah, I don't think so.

70
00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.940
This kid looks like
a real charmer, too.

71
00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.180
[LUFFY]
Like your face?

72
00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.940
You wanna fight, you little punk?

73
00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:22.600
So rude!

74
00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.440
[DOGRA, MAGRA]
– Dadan!
– Dadan!

75
00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:25.080
[DOGRA]
Don't let him get to you!

76
00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:25.950
What the heck?

77
00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:26.650
Ew!

78
00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:27.570
Spit!

79
00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:28.940
That's gross!

80
00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:30.840
Who did that?

81
00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:31.840
Hey!

82
00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.340
You jerk!

83
00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:35.210
You better apologize for that!

84
00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.340
Hey!

85
00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:37.550
There he is!

86
00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.110
Oh, hello, Ace, welcome back!

87
00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:45.320
<b>Portgas D. Ace








(10 Years Ago)</b>

88
00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.550
I'm waiting!

89
00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.610
[GARP]
Luffy, This here is Ace.

90
00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.410
He's three years older than you.

91
00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:56.650
Anyway, you're gonna be living
with him and Dadan from now on.

92
00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:59.980
What? Not so fast!

93
00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:06.140
You play nice.

94
00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:07.710
We said, "No"!

95
00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:09.480
You'll do it.

96
00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.380
Sir, as you wish, sir!

97
00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:15.970
[BANDIT GG]
It's your turn to do the dishes.

98
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.200
[LUFFY]
Old man.

99
00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.030
Can I have some more?

100
00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:21.000
I'm a woman, thank you very much!

101
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.910
Do you even know where you are
right now, you filthy little urchin?

102
00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:24.610
[LUFFY]
Nope.

103
00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:25.910
Okay, then I'll tell you.

104
00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:29.970
This is the den of the Dadan Family...
mountain bandits that rule Mount Corvo!

105
00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.340
Mountain bandits?

106
00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:32.080
Bluh.

107
00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.550
Mountain bandits are lame.

108
00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.980
Well, you're stuck with us!

109
00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:40.410
Or rather, we're stuck with you,
thanks to that pushy grandfather of yours!

110
00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:42.380
But if you don't want to stay,
that's fine by me...

111
00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.820
go get eaten by a bunch
of wolves for all I care!

112
00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:46.880
Easy, Boss. Easy.

113
00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.350
I just wanted s'more rice.

114
00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:51.150
[LUFFY]
Or meat.

115
00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:53.190
Meat would be nice.

116
00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:03.730
In case you didn't notice, all this meat
came from that bison Ace brought back.

117
00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:07.110
Even though he's a kid like you,
he has to work to earn his keep.

118
00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.180
The bandit life's a hard one, boy.

119
00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:12.790
Tomorrow, you're gonna pay
in blood, sweat, and tears:

120
00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:16.570
Cleaning, doing laundry,
polishing our boots and weapons,

121
00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:19.890
robbery, fraud, murder, and terror!

122
00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:22.540
And if you go crying
to your dear old grandpa,

123
00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.070
we'll string you up
without a second thought!

124
00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:29.610
One bowl of rice and one glass of water,
that's all I can promise you.

125
00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.980
The rest you get for yourself.

126
00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:34.180
You're gonna have
to grow up real fast, kid.

127
00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.190
Or you'll go hungry
before the week's up.

128
00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:37.250
No problem.

129
00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:40.390
"No problem"? Not crying
and begging for mercy?

130
00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:44.210
Grandpa threw me in the jungle one time,
so I know how to tough it out just fine.

131
00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:46.940
There's plenty of water to drink
and I can eat frogs and snakes

132
00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:49.520
and mushrooms and stuff all I want.

133
00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:53.290
I'm gonna be a pirate someday,
so I gotta be strong!

134
00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.940
This is gonna be real fun!

135
00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:56.650
[BANDIT HH]
Boss!

136
00:07:56.650 --> 00:07:57.510
[BANDIT II]
You okay?

137
00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:59.050
[BANDIT JJ]
Hurry! Help her up!

138
00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:01.580
[BANDITS]
Heave-ho!

139
00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:03.110
Huh.

140
00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:04.140
Why is he leaving?

141
00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.940
[BANDITS]
One more!

142
00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:08.480
Hey, get back here, you!

143
00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:11.150
Hold on, what d'you mean
you're gonna be a pirate?

144
00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:13.150
And stop ignoring me!

145
00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:14.390
[LUFFY]
Hey!

146
00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.160
He just got here,
and he's already a pain!

147
00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:23.030
It's gonna be like having
a baby Garp living with us!

148
00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:26.020
Now, now, it's okay!

149
00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.660
[LUFFY]
Hey!

150
00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:29.690
Wait for me!

151
00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.560
Hey!

152
00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:35.600
Hi!

153
00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:37.030
My name's Luffy!

154
00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.330
Everything's cool now!

155
00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.970
I'm not mad about you spitting on me!

156
00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:45.000
[laughs]

157
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.820
Why are you all laughing?

158
00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:49.220
But the guy just spilled
some booze on me.

159
00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.460
It's not worth getting
bent out of shape.

160
00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.460
It's not worth getting
bent out of shape!

161
00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.660
I'd rather be friends!

162
00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.560
So, can I come with you?

163
00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:09.110
[DOGRA]
Huh? Wait. You're alone?

164
00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:10.380
That's not good.

165
00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:11.340
Uh, yeah.

166
00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.050
Where's Luffy?

167
00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:14.250
Wasn't he with you?

168
00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:15.210
Beats me.

169
00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.330
Get a hold of yourself!

170
00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:19.760
This is serious!

171
00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:20.800
No biggie.

172
00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.670
Oh, and is that what
you're gonna say to Garp

173
00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:24.700
when he finds out we
let his grandson die?

174
00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:25.570
Why do you care?

175
00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:27.700
One less crappy brat in the world.

176
00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:29.500
[DADAN]
Y'know what?

177
00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:32.970
While we're at it, screw Ace, too!

178
00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:37.170
[DADAN]
If he dies, we'll
tell Garp it was an accident.

179
00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:39.980
I mean, that'd be
the truth, wouldn't it?

180
00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:41.980
The devil's children
have the devil's luck!

181
00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:43.010
How 'bout that?

182
00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:46.220
'Cause Ace is
the devil's son, for sure.

183
00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:49.750
What do you think the Government
would do if they found out about him?

184
00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:50.520
Hah!

185
00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:51.990
I'll take my chances with Garp!

186
00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:54.660
[MAGRA]
Hey, you don't mean that, Boss.

187
00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.830
[DOGRA]
Come on, that's the booze talking.

188
00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.690
Just sleep it off.

189
00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:02.680
[NARRATOR]
One week later.

190
00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:02.940
[shrieks]

191
00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:05.450
Boss! Wake up! C'mere, quick!

192
00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:07.980
[DADAN]
What?

193
00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:09.480
Oh!

194
00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:10.590
It's you!

195
00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:12.390
[DOGRA]
The little bugger isn't dead after all!

196
00:11:12.390 --> 00:11:13.990
[barking]

197
00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:20.410
You're alive.

198
00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:22.450
Why'd you scare us like that?

199
00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:23.150
Huh?

200
00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:24.650
Easy, easy, Boss.

201
00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:26.650
Where the hell were you,
and what were you doing?

202
00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:30.560
Now, now, just give him a second... he'll
answer without all the face stretching.

203
00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:34.320
I was stuck at the bottom of the
valley getting chased by wolves.

204
00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:35.390
Are you nuts?

205
00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:38.620
What the heck were you
trying to do down there?

206
00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:41.680
[DOGRA]
Well, whatever.

207
00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:43.720
It's good you came back safe.

208
00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.730
There's nothing good about it!

209
00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:48.230
Another useless mouth to feed!

210
00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:50.430
Get some sleep while you can.

211
00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:53.600
We're putting you to work
bright and early tomorrow!

212
00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:05.280
Hey, Ace!

213
00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:07.210
You going somewhere fun today?

214
00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:08.550
Take me!

215
00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:12.820
I know I was gone for a while,
but I still wanna be friends!

216
00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:13.990
Wait!

217
00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:16.730
[DOGRA]
Boss! He's running after Ace again!

218
00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:17.730
Hey!

219
00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:21.400
Get back here...you
still have chores to do!

220
00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.200
Nyah! I'm outta here!

221
00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.800
I am gonna wring your
rotten neck, you twerp!

222
00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:28.940
Easy, easy!

223
00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:31.010
You shut your yapper
and go bring him back!

224
00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:31.940
[MAGRA]
Yes, ma'am.

225
00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:54.330
[NARRATOR]
It was the same thing every time.

226
00:12:56.530 --> 00:12:57.600
[LUFFY screams]

227
00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:59.870
[NARRATOR]
But that didn't deter him one bit.

228
00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:01.370
[LUFFY]
Ace!

229
00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.880
[NARRATOR]
A month passed.

230
00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:14.380
Two months.

231
00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:15.790
[LUFFY]
Wait up!

232
00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:17.890
[NARRATOR]
In the rain.

233
00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:19.520
Or in the wind.

234
00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:20.220
[LUFFY shrieks]

235
00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:21.860
[gasps]

236
00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.790
[LUFFY]
Let's be friends!

237
00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:26.900
[NARRATOR]
Ace would run
and Luffy would chase him.

238
00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:49.520
I'm having a tough
time losing him today.

239
00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:51.190
Stubborn punk.

240
00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.330
Uh-oh!

241
00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:55.010
Crap!

242
00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:55.960
[LUFFY]
This sucks!

243
00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:57.030
Got away again!

244
00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:59.270
How'd he get so darn fast?

245
00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:02.570
Hey, there you are!

246
00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.610
[screams]

247
00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:13.040
[ACE]
That's gotta be the
nastiest monster in the forest.

248
00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.210
Even I can't beat that thing!

249
00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:19.080
[ACE]
Run away, stupid!

250
00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.410
It's gonna eat you!

251
00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:31.250
[NARRATOR]
Three months had passed, and although

252
00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:36.010
he was covered with cuts and
bruises, Luffy did not relent.

253
00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:45.530
[LUFFY]
The end of the forest.

254
00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.240
What is this place?!

255
00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:57.660
[NARRATOR]
On the North side of Mount Corvo,
not far from where Dadan's bandits live,

256
00:15:57.660 --> 00:16:00.360
there is a surprise
at the end of the forest.

257
00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:05.740
Covered in a thick mist, piles
of trash reach toward the heavens.

258
00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:09.240
It is a place where
the unwanted gather.

259
00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:12.840
That goes for the refuse as well
as those who reside there,

260
00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:15.510
rogues cast out by society.

261
00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:17.680
It is a den of lawlessness.

262
00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:23.020
Crime and disease run rampant, with
neither Marines nor doctors present.

263
00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:27.280
This place is known as "Gray Terminal."

264
00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:29.010
Just a bunch of junk.

265
00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:30.450
Gotta be something.

266
00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:32.280
Come on.

267
00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:35.080
Ha!

268
00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:36.520
Finally!

269
00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:37.390
[MAN C]
Fork it over!

270
00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:38.750
[MAN D]
Yeah, right! That's mine!

271
00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:39.610
[MAN B]
Screw you!

272
00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:41.340
I found it!

273
00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:43.210
You're gonna break it, you idiots!

274
00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:45.480
[MAN E]
It's cool man,
I just wanna cash it in for you!

275
00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:47.210
[MAN B]
Yeah, right!

276
00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:49.310
[MAN C]
C'mon, just gimme one pearl!

277
00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.980
[gasps]

278
00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:59.390
Back off!

279
00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.060
You can only blame yourself.

280
00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:06.340
Next time, let's try this
without all the running.

281
00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:07.010
Huh?

282
00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:09.010
Look what I found!

283
00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:10.010
No way!

284
00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:12.510
Get back here!

285
00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:15.850
[MAN C]
Thief!

286
00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:21.430
Hey!

287
00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:23.100
Move it, you brat!

288
00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:25.900
What is your problem?

289
00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:27.870
You want some of this?

290
00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:29.370
[MAN C]
He went that way!

291
00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:36.740
Sabo!

292
00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:38.710
Hey, are you up there?

293
00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:40.380
[SABO grunts]

294
00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:43.080
Oh. What's up, Ace?

295
00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.750
[ACE]
Sorry I'm a little late this time.

296
00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.590
[SABO]
More than "a little." I went out there.

297
00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:51.290
<b>Sabo (Age 10)








(A Boy Living in Gray Terminal)</b>

298
00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:50.190
and made a killing already today.

299
00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:51.520
Heh.

300
00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:52.530
[ACE]
Heh.

301
00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:53.630
Oh yeah?

302
00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:55.360
Well, maybe I did too.

303
00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:57.290
[SABO, ACE]
– Let's see!
– Let's see!

304
00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:58.830
Whoa! Dude!

305
00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:00.460
You got more than me!

306
00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:02.530
That's a ton of cash!

307
00:18:02.530 --> 00:18:03.970
What happened?

308
00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:05.770
Some chumps near the gate.

309
00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:07.800
Robbed 'em blind and made a run for it.

310
00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:09.430
Hah! Well, crap!

311
00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:11.230
Guess you win again, buddy!

312
00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:13.530
It doesn't matter
if you "win" or "lose."

313
00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:17.170
We've got five years of
"pirate savings" piled up.

314
00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:20.170
We should both be happy about that.

315
00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:25.420
We worked pretty hard.

316
00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:28.090
Yeah, no kidding.

317
00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:32.790
We'll leave this dump behind and go
places these chumps never even dreamed of.

318
00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:34.630
This is all gonna be worth it.

319
00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.190
Just you wait.

320
00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:43.880
We'd better put it away now.

321
00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:45.820
We can't let anyone else see this.

322
00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:47.550
So how much is a ship?

323
00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:50.320
I want a good one, but
seems like we're pretty rich.

324
00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:51.250
Yeah?

325
00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:54.060
Could take 10 million, maybe even more.

326
00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:55.530
Shouldn't rush it.

327
00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:59.000
[LUFFY]
Did you say "ship"?
You're gonna be pirates?

328
00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.620
And you've got hidden treasure already?

329
00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:05.890
I'm gonna be a pirate too! Yay!

330
00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:09.090
[giggles]

331
00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:17.240
[SABO, ACE growl]
– Shut up!
– Shut up!

332
00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:20.940
Know what's cool?

333
00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:24.070
Now that I know where you go,
I can follow you every day!

334
00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:25.110
[ACE]
Great.

335
00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:26.740
Luffy, huh?

336
00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:28.810
This is the brat you
were talking about.

337
00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:29.970
Huh?!

338
00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:31.640
Does that mean you
told your friends about me?

339
00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:34.400
I was telling my friend
how annoying you were.

340
00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:37.410
[SABO]
He also told me that
your head's full of rocks.

341
00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:39.870
[laughs]
Head rocks!

342
00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:42.880
You do realize we're messing
with you here, right?

343
00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:45.510
The route I took here
wasn't easy to follow.

344
00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:48.680
I knew he was hard-headed, but
I didn't think he was so tough.

345
00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:51.180
So great that Ace
has other friends too!

346
00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:53.260
I bet we're all gonna be best pals!

347
00:19:53.260 --> 00:19:54.630
[SABO]
I'm not your "pal."

348
00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.700
You don't even know my name, stupid!

349
00:19:56.700 --> 00:19:57.370
'Kay.

350
00:19:57.370 --> 00:19:58.670
Then what is your name?

351
00:19:58.670 --> 00:19:59.670
[SABO]
It's Sa...

352
00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:01.170
a secret!

353
00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:02.730
I told you, didn't I?

354
00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:04.240
You need to live here!

355
00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:09.020
The mountains made you tough, but at this
rate, our whole plan's gonna be ruined.

356
00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:11.890
What now?

357
00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:13.710
[ACE]
He knows our secret.

358
00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:16.310
We can't trust him
to keep his mouth shut.

359
00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:18.880
He's too stupid.

360
00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:24.590
We'll kill him.

361
00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:25.560
Yep.

362
00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:26.560
Sounds good.

363
00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:28.580
[gasps]

364
00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:31.450
No!

365
00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:33.620
Stop, this is scary!

366
00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:35.680
Somebody help me!

367
00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:37.450
I don't wanna die!

368
00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:39.190
[SABO]
Gimme a break! This kid is the worst!

369
00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:40.460
Just kill 'im already!

370
00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:41.460
Hurry it up!

371
00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:43.490
He's your problem...
why don't you do it?

372
00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:45.830
Because I've never killed
anyone before, okay?

373
00:20:45.830 --> 00:20:47.160
Well, neither have I!

374
00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:48.660
I don't know how this crap works!

375
00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:53.130
[ACE]
Okay! The river!

376
00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:55.560
[SABO]
That's convenient,
but why did he say that?

377
00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:56.630
[ACE]
I told you, he's stupid!

378
00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:59.130
Somebody help me!

379
00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:00.630
[SABO, ACE]
– That's enough!
– That's enough!

380
00:21:02.930 --> 00:21:04.930
Don't kill me!

381
00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:06.330
[HOODLUM A]
Wait listen.

382
00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:07.570
I just heard some screaming.

383
00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:08.810
Sounded like a kid.

384
00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:09.770
Aw, damn it.

385
00:21:09.770 --> 00:21:11.310
Somebody heard him!

386
00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:12.180
Set him free.

387
00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:13.700
We gotta get outta here and fast.

388
00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:17.010
If people start snooping around,
they'll find our treasure.

389
00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:23.700
Sounds like you're talking about Ace and
Sabo... those two're infamous around here.

390
00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:28.340
<b>Porchemy







Bluejam Pirates</b>

391
00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:25.700
And the one who took your money.

392
00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:26.970
That was Ace, right?

393
00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.640
The kid who had the
black hair, you said?

394
00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:29.670
Uh-huh.

395
00:21:29.670 --> 00:21:31.380
This is real pathetic, I know.

396
00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:32.880
We both got sloppy.

397
00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:35.040
He's either cocky or dumb.

398
00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:38.380
You can't rob pirates blind
and expect to get away with it.

399
00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:40.410
Bottom line is, if we
don't get that money back,

400
00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:44.410
Captain Bluejam's gonna skin
us alive, and I mean literally.

401
00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:46.780
[ACE]
Bluejam?

402
00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.020
Crap!

403
00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:50.180
How was I s'posed to know
they were workin' with him?

404
00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:51.620
You robbed those guys?

405
00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:53.650
Are you trying to
get us killed or what?

406
00:21:53.650 --> 00:21:54.560
[ACE]
Yeah.

407
00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:57.210
This is not gonna end well.

408
00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:58.510
[SABO]
That sword looks sharp.

409
00:21:58.510 --> 00:22:00.510
though you probably saw that already.

410
00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:03.690
The guy with 'em is Porchemy.

411
00:22:03.690 --> 00:22:05.520
He's crazy.

412
00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:07.260
Lose a fight with him.

413
00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:10.530
And he'll scalp you alive
just to hear you scream.

414
00:22:13.860 --> 00:22:16.730
Just lay low and
let 'em pass by for now.

415
00:22:18.030 --> 00:22:18.870
Uh-oh.

416
00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:20.200
He's gone.

417
00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:24.140
You better put me down
right now, you big jerk!

418
00:22:24.140 --> 00:22:26.410
[SABO, ACE]
– How did he get caught already?
– How did he get caught already?

419
00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:28.740
Who the hell is this?

420
00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:29.980
This guy won't put me down!

421
00:22:29.980 --> 00:22:32.950
Ace, help!

422
00:22:32.950 --> 00:22:34.580
Ace! Why aren't you saving me?

423
00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:35.280
We're friends, right?

424
00:22:35.280 --> 00:22:36.950
We should've killed him.

425
00:22:36.950 --> 00:22:38.750
Now we're all dead!

426
00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:43.510
So, you know Ace, do ya?

427
00:22:43.510 --> 00:22:44.670
Yeah, that's right.

428
00:22:44.670 --> 00:22:48.310
And if you cry, do ya
think he'll come for ya?

429
00:22:49.140 --> 00:22:51.550
Yeah, 'cause we're friends.

430
00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:55.580
Except he just tried
to kill me, so maybe not.

431
00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:56.420
Shut up!

432
00:22:56.420 --> 00:22:58.750
Are you kidding me?

433
00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:00.820
[PORCHEMY]
If he's your friend,
maybe you can help us.

434
00:23:00.820 --> 00:23:02.750
See, Ace stole our money.

435
00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:06.250
And if we got it back, we
wouldn't have to hurt anybody.

436
00:23:06.250 --> 00:23:09.320
You don't happen to
know where it is, do ya?

437
00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:14.990
[SABO]
We're screwed!

438
00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:17.260
They're gonna take
our treasure for sure!

439
00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:20.040
For once in your life, please shut up.

440
00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:31.040
I don't know!

441
00:23:31.040 --> 00:23:32.910
Sorry.

442
00:23:32.910 --> 00:23:34.640
[PORCHEMY]
What a crappy liar!

443
00:23:38.840 --> 00:23:40.210
All right, fine.

444
00:23:40.210 --> 00:23:43.010
I'm sure you just forgot.

445
00:23:44.240 --> 00:23:46.010
[chuckles]

446
00:23:46.010 --> 00:23:49.680
Don't worry, I have ways
of jogging your memory.

447
00:23:50.850 --> 00:23:52.180
[LUFFY]
I told you I don't know!

448
00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:54.350
Let go of me, you dumb jerk!

449
00:23:54.350 --> 00:23:56.520
Ace is gonna kick your butt,
I'm telling you!

450
00:23:56.520 --> 00:23:57.910
You're in big

451
00:23:58.240 --> 00:23:59.740
'Kay, so now what?

452
00:23:59.740 --> 00:24:01.240
Stop asking me!

453
00:24:01.240 --> 00:24:02.810
You know what!

454
00:24:11.120 --> 00:24:12.760
Lemme go!

455
00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:15.430
I'm not telling you a darn thing!

456
00:24:22.970 --> 00:24:24.840
You little punk!

457
00:24:32.180 --> 00:24:33.520
[shocked noises]

458
00:24:39.060 --> 00:24:42.960
The Gum-Gum Fruit turned me into rubber,
so that stuff's not gonna work on me!

459
00:24:42.960 --> 00:24:45.660
Calm down!

460
00:24:45.660 --> 00:24:47.800
A Devil Fruit, huh?

461
00:24:47.800 --> 00:24:49.330
Heh.

462
00:24:49.330 --> 00:24:51.800
I know how to deal with that.

463
00:24:53.630 --> 00:24:56.270
Bring me my pair of gloves.

464
00:24:56.270 --> 00:24:58.100
[HOODLUM B]
Y-Yes, sir!

465
00:24:58.100 --> 00:24:58.770
[SABO]
Hurry, man!

466
00:24:58.770 --> 00:24:59.800
Faster!

467
00:24:59.800 --> 00:25:01.470
We're screwed if those guys come back!

468
00:25:01.470 --> 00:25:04.660
We gotta move all this,
but I don't know where.

469
00:25:04.660 --> 00:25:08.640
Luffy's pretty stubborn, but it's only
a matter of time before he rats us out.

470
00:25:08.640 --> 00:25:11.980
I'm not losing our pirate savings
to those jerks, or anyone else!

471
00:25:11.980 --> 00:25:13.970
It took us five years
to score all this!

472
00:25:13.970 --> 00:25:16.440
We can't get stuck
in this dump forever!

473
00:25:21.450 --> 00:25:23.350
I'll try to clear this up a little.

474
00:25:23.350 --> 00:25:25.950
The money Ace stole isn't
just some chump change,

475
00:25:25.950 --> 00:25:29.390
it's a matter of life and death
for me and all of my buddies here.

476
00:25:29.390 --> 00:25:32.530
And you're gonna tell me where it is.

477
00:25:32.530 --> 00:25:36.400
Even if I gotta beat it outta you.

478
00:25:36.400 --> 00:25:38.100
Will not!

479
00:25:46.010 --> 00:25:47.510
That's rough!

480
00:25:51.110 --> 00:25:54.280
I'm warnin' you, kid.
You don't piss off a pirate.

481
00:25:54.280 --> 00:25:59.490
If I don't kick your ass, Captain Bluejam's
gonna kill you and all of us, too.

482
00:26:05.030 --> 00:26:06.900
[LUFFY screams]
Let me go!

483
00:26:06.900 --> 00:26:09.030
You're hurting me!

484
00:26:09.030 --> 00:26:10.730
Somebody help!

485
00:26:13.800 --> 00:26:15.770
[PORCHEMY]
We don't have time
to stand around, you idiots!

486
00:26:15.770 --> 00:26:18.770
Go look for Ace and Sabo while
I take care of this one!

487
00:26:18.770 --> 00:26:20.270
[HOODLUMS Yes, sir!

488
00:26:28.210 --> 00:26:29.780
[MAN H]
Ace and Sabo, huh?

489
00:26:29.780 --> 00:26:31.250
Yeah. I know 'em.

490
00:26:31.250 --> 00:26:32.220
Oh, I get it.

491
00:26:32.220 --> 00:26:34.880
You're from the city.

492
00:26:34.880 --> 00:26:36.620
Leave those two be.

493
00:26:36.620 --> 00:26:38.780
If you were locals, you'd understand.

494
00:26:38.780 --> 00:26:41.280
They may be kids,
but they're also crazy.

495
00:26:41.280 --> 00:26:44.550
Yeah, man, they got claws
like a tiger, if you cross 'em.

496
00:26:44.550 --> 00:26:46.250
Ace and Sabo, huh?

497
00:26:46.250 --> 00:26:48.380
I wouldn't know.

498
00:26:48.380 --> 00:26:50.720
But while we're
having this little chat.

499
00:26:50.720 --> 00:26:53.450
Why don't you boys
fork over your wallets?

500
00:26:53.450 --> 00:26:55.420
We... We don't want any trouble!

501
00:26:55.420 --> 00:26:57.290
We'll ask someone else!

502
00:27:00.950 --> 00:27:03.390
[ACE]
Didn't realize it was getting so late.

503
00:27:03.390 --> 00:27:04.090
All right!

504
00:27:04.090 --> 00:27:05.590
I finally did it!

505
00:27:05.590 --> 00:27:08.090
Not even Luffy knows about this spot!

506
00:27:11.520 --> 00:27:12.480
I'm back!

507
00:27:12.480 --> 00:27:13.450
[ACE]
Hmm?

508
00:27:13.450 --> 00:27:14.650
I moved everything.

509
00:27:14.650 --> 00:27:15.590
What happened?

510
00:27:15.590 --> 00:27:17.620
Are they poking
around at the old place?

511
00:27:20.190 --> 00:27:22.090
No, that's the thing.

512
00:27:22.090 --> 00:27:25.120
Bluejam's guys are
still out looking for us!

513
00:27:25.120 --> 00:27:26.320
And what does that mean?

514
00:27:26.320 --> 00:27:28.950
I'm telling you, it's Luffy!

515
00:27:29.650 --> 00:27:32.560
All that time and
he still didn't rat us out!

516
00:27:33.490 --> 00:27:35.890
I thought he would,
since he's such an idiot.

517
00:27:35.890 --> 00:27:38.490
That, and he was crying
whenever we left him.

518
00:27:38.490 --> 00:27:40.490
But you know what
this means, don't you?

519
00:27:40.490 --> 00:27:42.500
They're torturing him right now!

520
00:27:44.020 --> 00:27:46.320
What if he still doesn't talk?

521
00:27:52.950 --> 00:27:57.230
<b>Gray Terminal








Pirate Bay</b>

522
00:27:54.800 --> 00:27:57.660
[BLUEJAM]
Getting awful late, isn't it?

523
00:27:57.660 --> 00:28:00.860
Who did I leave in charge today?

524
00:28:00.860 --> 00:28:04.760
Well, Captain Bluejam, if I
recall, it should be Porchemy.

525
00:28:04.760 --> 00:28:07.700
Huh. Then he'd better hurry.

526
00:28:09.090 --> 00:28:12.060
Well, surely they made the sale.

527
00:28:12.060 --> 00:28:14.900
It couldn't have taken them that long.

528
00:28:14.900 --> 00:28:19.370
Maybe Porchemy thinks he's clever
enough to take my money and skip town.

529
00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:18.970
<b>Captain Bluejam








Bluejam Pirates</b>

530
00:28:19.370 --> 00:28:21.040
Of course not, Captain!

531
00:28:21.040 --> 00:28:24.910
I doubt he would throw his life
away for some measly treasure.

532
00:28:24.910 --> 00:28:26.410
Ah...

533
00:28:26.410 --> 00:28:28.160
Let's hope not.

534
00:28:28.410 --> 00:28:32.720
[punching sounds]

535
00:28:32.720 --> 00:28:35.520
[PORCHEMY]
C'mon, kid, spit it out.

536
00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:40.360
W-Wait.

537
00:28:40.360 --> 00:28:41.730
Porchemy, stop it.

538
00:28:41.730 --> 00:28:43.690
I don't think he's gonna talk.

539
00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:48.170
He's shutting down.

540
00:28:48.170 --> 00:28:51.040
The kid's not even
calling for help anymore.

541
00:28:54.970 --> 00:28:57.330
If he was gonna talk,
he would've done it already.

542
00:28:57.330 --> 00:29:00.460
And to be honest, this is
getting kinda hard to watch.

543
00:29:00.460 --> 00:29:02.970
Show the little bastard some mercy!

544
00:29:05.970 --> 00:29:10.100
If you have time to bitch about this,
then you have time to go look for Ace!

545
00:29:10.100 --> 00:29:14.270
We're the ones who're gonna get
killed here, not the damn kid!

546
00:29:14.270 --> 00:29:17.180
Save your breath, 'cause
you'll be begging for mercy

547
00:29:17.180 --> 00:29:20.090
from Captain Bluejam soon enough!

548
00:29:24.680 --> 00:29:26.120
They're gonna kill that child.

549
00:29:26.120 --> 00:29:28.950
Do you think we should call
the sheriff from the city?

550
00:29:28.950 --> 00:29:30.220
There's no point.

551
00:29:30.220 --> 00:29:32.850
I mean, this place doesn't
fall under any country's laws.

552
00:29:32.850 --> 00:29:36.630
Plus, that Porchemy guy's a
member of the Bluejam Pirates.

553
00:29:36.630 --> 00:29:38.630
They're paying off
the nobles, you know.

554
00:29:39.630 --> 00:29:42.730
So, in other words, even if they
do get arrested for a crime,

555
00:29:42.730 --> 00:29:44.630
they're just gonna be
pardoned in the end.

556
00:29:44.630 --> 00:29:48.340
Besides, what's one more dead
body in a place like this?

557
00:29:48.340 --> 00:29:50.010
Nobody gives a damn.

558
00:29:51.300 --> 00:29:52.900
Answer me!

559
00:29:54.700 --> 00:29:56.440
I'm not talking.

560
00:29:57.040 --> 00:29:58.310
[PORCHEMY]
You little punk!

561
00:29:58.310 --> 00:30:01.210
I'll beat that secret out
of you, or I'll beat you dead!

562
00:30:05.320 --> 00:30:07.520
Tell me!

563
00:30:10.360 --> 00:30:12.690
I won't do it.

564
00:30:12.690 --> 00:30:14.730
I won't talk.

565
00:30:14.730 --> 00:30:17.100
Just let me go.

566
00:30:20.100 --> 00:30:23.040
[LUFFY]
I'm not telling you.

567
00:30:23.820 --> 00:30:24.790
Fine.

568
00:30:24.790 --> 00:30:26.520
Enough of this.

569
00:30:44.680 --> 00:30:46.480
We're finished here, brat.

570
00:31:03.010 --> 00:31:04.310
It's that damn kid!

571
00:31:04.310 --> 00:31:05.580
He's got the money!

572
00:31:05.580 --> 00:31:06.580
That brat!

573
00:31:06.580 --> 00:31:07.380
[growls]

574
00:31:07.380 --> 00:31:08.380
Huh?

575
00:31:08.380 --> 00:31:11.080
Ace! You're here!

576
00:31:11.080 --> 00:31:14.380
[ACE roars]

577
00:31:16.120 --> 00:31:17.560
[PORCHEMY]
Thanks for showin' up, kid.

578
00:31:17.560 --> 00:31:19.790
You saved us some trouble.

579
00:31:19.790 --> 00:31:20.990
Your friend ain't squealin'.

580
00:31:20.990 --> 00:31:22.220
He's pretty tough.

581
00:31:22.220 --> 00:31:23.880
But I think you'll talk!

582
00:31:23.880 --> 00:31:24.650
Ace!

583
00:31:24.650 --> 00:31:28.050
S-Sabo... Do it!

584
00:31:32.460 --> 00:31:34.290
Boss, are you okay?

585
00:31:36.620 --> 00:31:38.860
Ace. Sabo.

586
00:31:38.860 --> 00:31:40.430
[PORCHEMY]
That kind of hurt.

587
00:31:40.430 --> 00:31:41.730
Who hit me?

588
00:31:41.730 --> 00:31:42.700
You?

589
00:31:44.200 --> 00:31:46.470
You punks don't get
who you're messing with!

590
00:31:46.470 --> 00:31:47.170
Yeah.

591
00:31:47.170 --> 00:31:48.840
You're all dead meat!

592
00:31:48.840 --> 00:31:50.700
[ACE]
Shut your mouth and fight!

593
00:31:50.700 --> 00:31:51.400
Sabo!

594
00:31:51.400 --> 00:31:52.310
Help Luffy!

595
00:31:52.310 --> 00:31:53.970
You guys.

596
00:31:54.670 --> 00:31:55.410
One thing.

597
00:31:55.410 --> 00:31:57.210
That ugly dude has a sword!

598
00:31:57.210 --> 00:31:58.810
Be careful!

599
00:32:10.760 --> 00:32:11.890
No way!

600
00:32:11.890 --> 00:32:14.190
Porchemy, that other
kid got our knife...!

601
00:32:17.400 --> 00:32:19.600
[SABO]
Quick, make a run for it!

602
00:32:19.600 --> 00:32:20.830
[ACE]
You go ahead!

603
00:32:20.830 --> 00:32:22.500
What? Ace!

604
00:32:22.500 --> 00:32:24.000
Let's just leave!

605
00:32:24.000 --> 00:32:26.070
[ACE]
I don't run from my enemies.

606
00:32:26.070 --> 00:32:26.870
Ever!

607
00:32:26.870 --> 00:32:28.500
Got it?

608
00:32:28.500 --> 00:32:31.110
[PORCHEMY]
And I don't go easy on my enemies!

609
00:32:31.110 --> 00:32:31.870
Come on!

610
00:32:31.870 --> 00:32:33.240
These guys aren't just thugs!

611
00:32:33.240 --> 00:32:34.600
They're Bluejam pirates!

612
00:32:34.600 --> 00:32:36.370
Yeah, you got that right!

613
00:32:36.370 --> 00:32:39.370
Now, I'm done playing games here.

614
00:32:39.370 --> 00:32:41.630
You've got something
that belongs to us.

615
00:32:41.630 --> 00:32:44.840
Be good and give it back, you brat!

616
00:32:44.840 --> 00:32:47.800
You're just a kid and I don't
blame you for actin' stupid,

617
00:32:47.800 --> 00:32:50.540
but fork over the cash
or you'll regret it.

618
00:32:52.500 --> 00:32:54.060
We've got better plans for it.

619
00:32:54.060 --> 00:32:56.070
That's our money now.

620
00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:00.700
Then you are dead!

621
00:33:00.700 --> 00:33:02.970
Hold on a sec, I'll be right back.

622
00:33:10.840 --> 00:33:13.300
I'm not gonna lose, ya hear?

623
00:33:13.300 --> 00:33:15.270
I'd rather just kill myself!

624
00:33:15.270 --> 00:33:18.240
Not if we do it first!

625
00:33:18.240 --> 00:33:20.180
Come at me, ya pricks!

626
00:33:29.180 --> 00:33:32.380
I heard the whole damn story, Porchemy.

627
00:33:32.380 --> 00:33:34.180
You should be ashamed.

628
00:33:34.180 --> 00:33:38.520
[BLUEJAM PIRATE]
Did you seriously get
beaten by a couple of kids?

629
00:33:38.520 --> 00:33:39.520
Yeah.

630
00:33:39.520 --> 00:33:41.990
Forgive me, Captain.

631
00:33:41.990 --> 00:33:42.720
The money...

632
00:33:42.720 --> 00:33:44.120
I've heard enough of this!

633
00:33:44.120 --> 00:33:45.790
You're not fit for my crew!

634
00:33:45.790 --> 00:33:48.460
[two gunshots]

635
00:33:57.780 --> 00:34:00.220
Ace, that was really not cool.

636
00:34:00.220 --> 00:34:02.160
Those guys were actual pirates!

637
00:34:02.160 --> 00:34:03.820
Next time, we run.

638
00:34:03.820 --> 00:34:07.090
Whatever your deal is,
it's not worth dying over.

639
00:34:07.090 --> 00:34:08.160
This sucks.

640
00:34:08.160 --> 00:34:11.420
I liked my old one better.

641
00:34:11.420 --> 00:34:12.420
[sighs]

642
00:34:12.420 --> 00:34:14.110
We made a huge mistake.

643
00:34:14.110 --> 00:34:16.180
Pissing off pirates like that, man.

644
00:34:16.180 --> 00:34:17.980
They probably told their captain.

645
00:34:17.980 --> 00:34:19.850
What are we supposed to do now?

646
00:34:19.850 --> 00:34:21.110
That was scary!

647
00:34:21.110 --> 00:34:24.210
I thought I was gonna die!

648
00:34:26.080 --> 00:34:27.220
[yells]

649
00:34:27.220 --> 00:34:28.380
Would you shut up?

650
00:34:28.380 --> 00:34:29.620
You're not hurt that bad!

651
00:34:29.620 --> 00:34:31.250
So, stop crying already!

652
00:34:31.250 --> 00:34:33.180
When're you gonna stop being a baby?

653
00:34:33.180 --> 00:34:35.690
Don't you want to be pirate?

654
00:34:37.860 --> 00:34:40.000
[LUFFY]
Th-Thank you!

655
00:34:45.140 --> 00:34:45.840
You...

656
00:34:45.840 --> 00:34:47.530
You saved me!

657
00:34:47.530 --> 00:34:48.330
Stop it!

658
00:34:48.330 --> 00:34:49.460
[SABO]
Calm down!

659
00:34:49.460 --> 00:34:51.700
He's just happy, okay?

660
00:34:54.740 --> 00:34:55.540
All right.

661
00:34:55.540 --> 00:34:56.580
What gives?

662
00:34:56.580 --> 00:34:58.400
Why didn't you tell
them what they wanted?

663
00:34:58.400 --> 00:35:00.940
You think they wouldn't kill
you 'cause you're a kid?

664
00:35:00.940 --> 00:35:03.430
Those guys don't give a damn!

665
00:35:03.430 --> 00:35:07.880
I was afraid... that you
wouldn't be my friend.

666
00:35:07.880 --> 00:35:09.280
Yeah? Well, so what?

667
00:35:09.280 --> 00:35:10.790
That still beats dying, right?

668
00:35:10.790 --> 00:35:13.170
Besides, why do you
want to be my friend?

669
00:35:13.170 --> 00:35:15.720
That's dumb!

670
00:35:15.720 --> 00:35:17.560
Because...

671
00:35:17.560 --> 00:35:19.160
[ACE]
It's not like I've been nice to you!

672
00:35:19.160 --> 00:35:21.700
In fact, I've been giving
you hell ever since we met!

673
00:35:21.700 --> 00:35:22.730
It's been months!

674
00:35:22.730 --> 00:35:24.500
Why haven't you just given up?

675
00:35:30.250 --> 00:35:31.590
[LUFFY]
Well...

676
00:35:31.590 --> 00:35:32.590
'Cause...

677
00:35:32.590 --> 00:35:35.690
'Cause I... I got no
one else to turn to!

678
00:35:35.690 --> 00:35:38.260
I can't go back to Windmill Village!

679
00:35:38.260 --> 00:35:40.530
I don't like the
mountain bandits, either!

680
00:35:40.530 --> 00:35:43.760
I'd be alone all the time
if I didn't follow you!

681
00:35:43.760 --> 00:35:48.030
Getting beat up hurts,
but being lonely hurts more!

682
00:35:48.830 --> 00:35:50.770
Alone? Why?

683
00:35:50.770 --> 00:35:53.100
Gramps is all I have.

684
00:35:54.320 --> 00:35:56.320
[ACE]
You feel better around me?

685
00:35:56.320 --> 00:35:57.920
Uh-huh.

686
00:35:57.920 --> 00:35:59.700
[ACE]
Otherwise you feel lonely?

687
00:35:59.700 --> 00:36:01.230
Uh-huh.

688
00:36:03.700 --> 00:36:06.200
[MAN A]
Do I think Gold Roger had a kid?

689
00:36:06.200 --> 00:36:07.600
[laughs]

690
00:36:07.600 --> 00:36:10.320
If he did, then too bad
for that poor runt!

691
00:36:10.320 --> 00:36:11.120
No kidding!

692
00:36:11.120 --> 00:36:12.480
They'd put him to death!

693
00:36:12.480 --> 00:36:14.430
He'd probably deserve it too!

694
00:36:14.430 --> 00:36:15.800
I bet!

695
00:36:21.630 --> 00:36:25.270
[ACE]
Do you think I deserve to live?

696
00:36:27.570 --> 00:36:28.330
[LUFFY]
Hmm?

697
00:36:28.330 --> 00:36:31.200
Of course I do!

698
00:36:31.200 --> 00:36:35.280
I see.

699
00:36:35.280 --> 00:36:36.610
But you're still annoying.

700
00:36:36.610 --> 00:36:39.310
Weak little crybabies piss me off.

701
00:36:40.650 --> 00:36:41.480
[LUFFY]
Nuh-uh.

702
00:36:41.480 --> 00:36:42.580
I'm not weak!

703
00:36:42.580 --> 00:36:44.080
I'm really strong!

704
00:36:44.080 --> 00:36:44.950
Ha!

705
00:36:44.950 --> 00:36:46.350
You think you're really strong?

706
00:36:46.350 --> 00:36:48.950
You were crying your eyes out
the whole time you were tied up!

707
00:36:48.950 --> 00:36:51.880
Have you ever gotten hit
by a spiky thing that big?

708
00:36:51.880 --> 00:36:53.350
I'm just seven years old!

709
00:36:53.350 --> 00:36:55.380
Wait till I turn ten
years old like you guys,

710
00:36:55.380 --> 00:36:58.170
and then I'll be stronger
and won't cry anymore!

711
00:36:58.170 --> 00:37:00.770
Age has nothing to
do with it, you brat!

712
00:37:00.770 --> 00:37:02.780
Hell, when I was seven I was tough!

713
00:37:02.780 --> 00:37:03.710
[LUFFY]
So what?

714
00:37:03.710 --> 00:37:05.480
I'm gonna be so tough you're gonna cry!

715
00:37:05.480 --> 00:37:09.270
I promised Shanks I'd be a great pirate
someday and that means way greater than you!

716
00:37:09.270 --> 00:37:11.050
[ACE]
Ha! You'll be a crappy pirate.

717
00:37:11.050 --> 00:37:11.650
[LUFFY]
Nuh-uh!

718
00:37:11.650 --> 00:37:12.350
[ACE]
Yeah-huh!

719
00:37:12.350 --> 00:37:13.180
[LUFFY]
Nuh-uh!

720
00:37:14.650 --> 00:37:17.050
Okay, enough of that!

721
00:37:17.680 --> 00:37:18.490
Jeez.

722
00:37:18.490 --> 00:37:19.550
Now, listen.

723
00:37:19.550 --> 00:37:22.020
In case you guys forgot,
we got a problem here.

724
00:37:22.020 --> 00:37:22.990
A problem?

725
00:37:24.540 --> 00:37:28.140
[SABO]
This forest where I've been living
is awfully close to their hideout.

726
00:37:28.140 --> 00:37:29.630
the Cove of Pirates.

727
00:37:29.630 --> 00:37:33.280
What if one night I'm a little too
tired, sleep a little too hard,

728
00:37:33.280 --> 00:37:34.980
and they sneak up on me?

729
00:37:53.990 --> 00:37:55.590
[DOGRA]
What's with all the bandages?

730
00:37:55.590 --> 00:37:58.230
Have they been fighting
bears or something?

731
00:38:00.400 --> 00:38:02.970
That's not the problem.

732
00:38:06.790 --> 00:38:07.990
[DOGRA]
Hey! Boss!

733
00:38:07.990 --> 00:38:09.020
Come quick!

734
00:38:09.020 --> 00:38:10.450
This isn't good!

735
00:38:10.450 --> 00:38:11.290
[DADAN]
Hmm?

736
00:38:11.290 --> 00:38:13.160
Gimme a sec, it's early.

737
00:38:13.160 --> 00:38:14.660
Huh?

738
00:38:14.660 --> 00:38:17.290
What have those brats been up to now?

739
00:38:17.290 --> 00:38:18.130
One.

740
00:38:18.130 --> 00:38:19.190
Two.

741
00:38:21.620 --> 00:38:24.960
Ace! Luffy! Who's
that other kid with you?

742
00:38:24.960 --> 00:38:26.160
[groans]

743
00:38:26.160 --> 00:38:28.020
Who's what now?

744
00:38:31.140 --> 00:38:33.950
[DADAN]
Ugh! Two brats is already too many!

745
00:38:33.950 --> 00:38:36.350
Who the hell are you?

746
00:38:36.350 --> 00:38:39.350
You mean me?

747
00:38:39.350 --> 00:38:40.050
Ah.

748
00:38:40.050 --> 00:38:41.120
Right!

749
00:38:41.120 --> 00:38:42.890
Hi! I'm Sabo!

750
00:38:42.890 --> 00:38:43.720
Huh?

751
00:38:43.720 --> 00:38:44.890
Ace's friend?

752
00:38:44.890 --> 00:38:46.020
I see.

753
00:38:46.020 --> 00:38:46.930
Oh, good!

754
00:38:46.930 --> 00:38:48.390
It's like I'm already living here!

755
00:38:48.390 --> 00:38:50.060
And you must be Dadan, right?

756
00:38:50.060 --> 00:38:51.520
Hiya!

757
00:38:51.520 --> 00:38:55.120
You're just as worthless as those
other two low-lifes moochin' off me!

758
00:38:55.120 --> 00:38:56.390
[SABO]
Oh, yeah?

759
00:38:56.390 --> 00:38:58.930
Well, I heard that you're
a worthless old hag yourself!

760
00:38:58.930 --> 00:39:00.700
[farts]

761
00:39:09.190 --> 00:39:11.390
[DADAN]
Luffy! Ace! Sabo!

762
00:39:11.390 --> 00:39:12.990
There aren't any free rides!

763
00:39:12.990 --> 00:39:15.760
You twerps better be grateful
and get to work this instant!

764
00:39:15.760 --> 00:39:17.030
[chuckles]

765
00:39:17.030 --> 00:39:19.030
You got it! Thank you!

766
00:39:29.380 --> 00:39:32.350
[NARRATOR]
Fearing for his life,
Sabo left Gray Terminal

767
00:39:32.350 --> 00:39:37.320
and found a home with Ace and
Luffy, much to Dadan's dismay.

768
00:39:37.320 --> 00:39:41.390
For the three unwanted guests,
it was a never-ending party.

769
00:39:41.390 --> 00:39:44.390
Making any excuse to get
out of their daily chores,

770
00:39:44.390 --> 00:39:48.930
they hunted wild animals in the mountains,
tussled with hooligans in the city,

771
00:39:48.930 --> 00:39:52.070
and dueled with pirates at the cove.

772
00:39:52.070 --> 00:39:56.340
Within time, news of their wild
exploits reached far and wide,

773
00:39:56.340 --> 00:39:59.610
even over the high walls surrounding
the center of the kingdom.
